          "text": "Headache"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent occipital/temporal pressure headache for 1–2 weeks, up to 6/10, worse on getting up from bed or bending. Episodes last minutes to 1 hour and settle with rest or Panadol. No photophobia, phonophobia, or aura."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Vertigo"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Vertigo for months, increased over the last 2 weeks. Triggered by rolling in bed, looking up, or lying flat, especially to the right. Described as the room spinning for a few seconds, lasting less than 30 seconds, and settling when the head is kept still. Similar to previous episodes."
      }
    },
